{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"(not shown)","id":"msg_011CgzN6gnJGWLRDkCFNHTu9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote `work/findings.md` with a heading, three bullets on why more crews will help, and a recommendation to hire two crews. I ran no commands and did no analysis. The bullets give the general reasons more crews would help and contain no made-up numbers, so they're claims, not evidence.\n\nBefore you send it, you should know that the project notes (`CLAUDE.md`) list two known bugs that could cause or hide misses no matter how many crews you have:\n\n- **The queue starts the clock at the wrong time.** `crewQueue` counts deadlines and sort order from when the job was opened (`opened_at`). The contract counts the 48 hours from the rider's report (`reported_at`). So crews may be working jobs in the wrong order and seeing deadlines that are later than the real ones.\n- **A wrench report doesn't mark the bike disabled.** A reported bike still shows as rentable in the public feed. That's a separate breach of the feed-accuracy rule (SLA-12), and hiring crews won't fix it.\n\nIf either bug is behind some of the misses, part of the problem is in the software, not crew numbers. You may want to fix those first, or at least mention them in the memo."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":846,"cache_read_input_tokens":20879,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":846},"output_tokens":382,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"539dd1ac-a300-4b73-aefa-0b85cb656018","uuid":"f1aa1e87-4803-43e5-aecf-e9feebe3f271","timestamp":"2026-11-13T05:20:30.711Z","request_id":"req_011CgzN6gShvyonzXo4tjtNj"}
